+  while higher values (e.g., `3`) increase it.
+  This allows setting preferred verbosity at compile time,
+  rather than passing `-q` or `-v` flags at runtime.
+  Example : `CPPFLAGS="-DZSTD_DISPLAY_LEVEL_DEFAULT=1" make`
